      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: well, no that's not true because bandit told me when i was learning to staff for furry talk and chill that his world got taken down before for making it so the ban panel could ban users automatically without the need for staff meaning it would detect the users in whatever instance they were in inside the furry talk and chill lobbies and ban them outright teleporting them to the ban area which the dev team took down his world for that. so i dont believe that what you said is ever true. it does detect instance type if you tinker with it. even if you're not in the world all the world owner needs to do is go into unity and type your name into the ban list and the world just needs to update for it to take effect and that doesnt include rejoining the instance.\n\nit just needs to read the code from the update for it to send you to the ban area.",
